<%
  page_data(
    title: "Calling the API",
    error: false,
    caption: "API developer documentation",
    caption_size: 'l'
  )
%>


<p class="govuk-body">
We have both application-restricted endpoints and user-restricted endpoints in the API.
</p>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">Application-restricted endpoints</h3>
<p class="govuk-body">
Application-restricted endpoints do not require authorisation from the end user. They do not give access to their sensitive data.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
We use application-restricted endpoints as a part of the authorisation process to generate an access token. These endpoints require that you authenticate the request using <%= govuk_link_to("HTTP Basic Authentication", "https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc7617/") %>
with your client ID and client secret.  To do this, add an HTTP header containing your credentials in the form <code>client_id:client_secret</code>, Base64 encoded.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
For example, if your client ID is <code>client123</code> and your secret is <code>supersecretvalue</code>, your Basic Authentication header would be:

<pre>
<code>
Authorization: Basic Y2xpZW50MTIzOnN1cGVyc2VjcmV0dmFsdWU=
</code>
</pre>
</p>

<%= govuk_warning_text(text: "Do not include your client ID or client secret in the body of the request.") %>


<p class="govuk-body">
We have a test <%= govuk_link_to("Hello API", api_hello_documentation_path, no_visited_state: true) %> where you can verify that you are correctly calling the API with your client credentials.
</p>

<h4 class="govuk-heading-s">Example request</h4>
<pre>
<code>
curl -X GET <%= @api_base_url %>/hello/client \
-H "Accept: application/json" \
-H "Authorization: Basic Y2xpZW50MTIzOnN1cGVyc2VjcmV0dmFsdWU="
</code>
</pre>


<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">User-restricted endpoints</h3>
<p class="govuk-body">
User-restricted endpoints give access to secure, personal data. To use them, your application must get permission from the end user.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
A user from each organisation you work with must authorise your application before we can give you an access token for that organisation.
</p>
<p class="govuk-body">
How to obtain an access token is discussed in the earlier sections of this documentation starting with <%= govuk_link_to("How authorisation works", api_documentation_authorisation_page_path("how-authorisation-works"), no_visited_state: true) %>. 
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
Once you have an access token you can access the user-restricted API endpoints. To do this, add an <code>Authorization</code> header to your request containing your access token as an OAuth 2.0 bearer token.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
You can verify that you are calling the API correctly with your access token using our <%= govuk_link_to("Hello API", api_hello_documentation_path, no_visited_state: true) %>.
</p>

<h4 class="govuk-heading-s">Example request</h4>

<pre>
<code>
curl -X GET <%= @api_base_url %>/hello/user \
-H "Accept: application/json" \
-H "Authorization: Bearer ZFfQMVBFJxyBdBhMqGzTdqMQPU23mVVu"
</code>
</pre>
